WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.594
- [Voiceover] I think
it was Macbeth who said,

00:00:01.594 --> 00:00:04.745
"If music be the spice
of life, then I love it!"

00:00:07.196 --> 00:00:08.223
Shoot.

00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:12.414
Either way, my allowance
of employees to listen

00:00:12.414 --> 00:00:15.110
to reasonably volumed
music means productivity

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.376
in the workplace has never been greater!

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:19.644
(driving hiphop)
- [Voiceover] Yeah, get it!

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:21.861
Damn, Drake, you done it again!

00:00:21.861 --> 00:00:24.393
I'm invincible with you by my side.

00:00:24.393 --> 00:00:26.449
Just stay away from that
Nicki Minaj, though, okay?

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:28.716
She's a bad influence on you, Bae.

00:00:31.761 --> 00:00:33.210
- [Voiceover] Take me from here,

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.405
(New Age vocalizing)
"Soundscapes", by Lana Fried!

00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:38.029
Oh, I'm so much more productive
when I picture myself

00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:41.048
in a Bengalese jungle, being waited on

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:44.075
hand and foot by day laborers.

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:45.876
This is the life!

00:00:50.336 --> 00:00:51.654
- [Voiceover] Have the keys
always been this close together?

00:00:51.654 --> 00:00:52.513
(dance music)
I'm thirsty.

00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:53.476
I'm doing good work today.

00:00:53.476 --> 00:00:54.892
Do I use my pinky or my ring finger less?

00:00:54.892 --> 00:00:55.809
This is good work.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:56.715
Coffee is good.

00:00:56.715 --> 00:00:57.977
Work is good. Things are good.

00:00:57.977 --> 00:00:58.935
Good working today, Anna.

00:00:58.935 --> 00:01:00.039
Good working!

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.296
(musical variety)
- [Voiceover] Yes!

00:01:05.296 --> 00:01:07.275
Yes, more music!

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:11.453
Coachella is happening in my cubicle!

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:14.833
Who's not cool enough
to get in a frat, now?

00:01:18.142 --> 00:01:19.113
- [Voiceover] Finally.

00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:20.245
It takes me putting on broken earbuds

00:01:20.245 --> 00:01:22.029
for these clowns to leave me alone.

00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:23.896
- Hey, did you hear the new...

00:01:23.896 --> 00:01:25.616
- [Voiceover] You're too thirsty, office.

00:01:25.616 --> 00:01:26.895
Too thirsty.

00:01:26.949 --> 00:01:30.071
- [Voiceover] Yes, music is
vital to our productivity.

00:01:30.071 --> 00:01:32.650
As for me, I don't need
to listen to music.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.263
It lives within me.

00:01:34.263 --> 00:01:36.243
I'm filled to the brim with it!

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:39.443
And I have been, ever since starring

00:01:39.443 --> 00:01:41.566
as Harold Hill in a gender-bent version

00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:44.893
of Meredith Willson's "The Music Man"!

00:01:44.893 --> 00:01:46.235
♫ We are in trouble, little guy

00:01:46.235 --> 00:01:48.568
♫ Right here, I say, trouble
right here in Creek Township

00:01:48.568 --> 00:01:49.783
♫ Why, I always had a tennis racket

00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:50.788
♫ Always had a tennis racket

00:01:50.788 --> 00:01:52.375
♫ Always had some trouble with it

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.210
♫ Do you say trouble, I say trouble

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.115
♫ Trouble, yes, trouble, no

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.528
♫ Trouble, yes, trouble, no

00:01:56.528 --> 00:01:57.427
- Does anyone else listen to music

00:01:57.427 --> 00:01:59.566
(frenzied singing continues)
just to drown out Natalie?

00:01:59.566 --> 00:02:00.408
- ♫ Trouble, trouble, trouble
- Yes.

00:02:00.408 --> 00:02:02.495
- [Voiceover] She sounds like my grandma.

00:02:02.495 --> 00:02:04.034
My grandma with asthma?
- ♫ Everyone likes trouble

00:02:04.034 --> 00:02:05.511
Ah, except us!

